1
00:00:11,500 --> 00:00:20,500
There are several types of chemical fume hoods that provide protection and help capture and exhaust chemical vapors and airborne particulates.
化学通风柜有好几种类型，它们都能提供防护，帮助捕集并排出化学蒸气和空气中的颗粒物。

2
00:00:20,500 --> 00:00:24,500
However, all types work on similar principles.
不过，所有类型的工作原理都相似。

3
00:00:24,500 --> 00:00:32,500
Air flow in a chemical fume hood can be interrupted, altered, and changed by different factors.
化学通风柜内的气流可能会因各种因素而被中断、改变和扰乱。

4
00:00:32,500 --> 00:00:40,500
Air flows into the hood capturing and containing contaminants, preventing them from escaping into the laboratory room.
空气流入通风柜，捕集并封闭污染物，防止它们逸散到实验室中。

5
00:00:40,500 --> 00:00:46,500
The smoke shown here provides visual demonstration of how air flows in a fume hood.
这里展示的烟雾直观地演示了通风柜内空气是如何流动的。

6
00:00:46,500 --> 00:00:53,880
Many conditions can affect the efficiency and safe operation of a fume hood.
许多情况都会影响通风柜的效率和安全运行。

7
00:00:53,880 --> 00:00:59,880
Chemicals closer to the front of the hood are more likely to leak from the hood.
越靠近通风柜前部的化学品，越容易从通风柜中泄漏出来。

8
00:00:59,880 --> 00:01:02,880
Operate at least six inches from the front.
操作时至少要距离前缘六英寸。

9
00:01:02,880 --> 00:01:10,880
The placement of objects close to the front opening may result in leakage and loss of containment.
把物品放在靠近前开口的地方，可能会导致泄漏和失去防护。

10
00:01:10,880 --> 00:01:19,880
Sash height is important for maintaining proper airflow and to keep those working in it and around it safe.
视窗高度对于维持正常气流、保障在通风柜内和周围工作的人员安全都很重要。

11
00:01:19,880 --> 00:01:24,880
When working in the hood, the sash should be at the certification mark.
在通风柜中工作时，视窗应处于认证标记的位置。

12
00:01:24,880 --> 00:01:29,880
Raising and lowering the sash should be done slowly.
升降视窗时应缓慢进行。

13
00:01:29,880 --> 00:01:35,880
Moving the sash quickly can disturb the airflow and result in leakage.
快速移动视窗会扰乱气流，导致泄漏。

14
00:01:35,880 --> 00:01:43,880
Large equipment inside the hood can obstruct the airflow and may allow vapors to escape into the lab.
通风柜内的大型设备会阻碍气流，可能使蒸气逸散到实验室中。

15
00:01:43,880 --> 00:01:52,880
Equipment should be elevated to allow air to flow under it so the proper fume hood airflow patterns will be maintained.
设备应垫高，让空气能从下面流过，从而保持通风柜正常的气流模式。

16
00:01:52,880 --> 00:01:58,880
Abrupt movements can cause turbulence allowing vapors to escape.
突然的动作会造成湍流，使蒸气逸出。

17
00:01:58,880 --> 00:02:08,880
For example, most people walk at a velocity of approximately 250 feet per minute, about three miles per hour.
例如，大多数人走路的速度约为每分钟 250 英尺，约每小时三英里。

18
00:02:08,880 --> 00:02:19,880
Wakes or vortices form behind a person who is walking, and the velocities in these vortices exceed 250 feet per minute.
行走的人身后会形成尾流或涡流，这些涡流中的速度会超过每分钟 250 英尺。

19
00:02:19,880 --> 00:02:33,880
When a person walks in front of an open fume hood, the vortices can overcome the fume hood face velocity and pull contaminants out of the fume hood, into the vortex, and into the laboratory.
当有人从敞开的通风柜前走过时，涡流可能会压过通风柜的面风速，把污染物从通风柜中拉出，卷入涡流，进入实验室。

20
00:02:33,880 --> 00:02:38,880
Place equipment and materials inside the hood before work begins.
开始工作前，把设备和材料放进通风柜。

21
00:02:38,880 --> 00:02:46,880
If you do need to move your arms out of the hood, move them slowly and perpendicular to the hood face.
如果确实需要把手臂移出通风柜，要缓慢地、垂直于通风柜开口面移动。

22
00:02:46,880 --> 00:02:56,880
The location of the hood is important too. It should be away from doors, fans, or ceiling air supply diffusers.
通风柜的位置也很重要。它应远离门、风扇或天花板送风散流器。

23
00:02:56,880 --> 00:03:00,880
The fume hood should be installed in a low traffic area.
通风柜应安装在人员走动较少的区域。
